ONE LINE: clean up keeps the tree short enough to read: history goes to git, cruft goes on a list Tony rules, and topic files stay inside a line budget.

/*****************************************************************************
    Description
*****************************************************************************/
Clean up is a session topic of its own (Tony, 2026-11-11). Its work is census, ruling, deletion: Clod counts and lists, Tony rules the list ("when in doubt, throw it out"), and what goes is tracked and pushed first, so git holds it.
The standing clean-as-you-go rule (CLAUDE.md): when a stroke of any topic turns up something that looks deletable, add an entry to docs/cleanupList.md and keep going; never act on it in flight. An entry names it and where, why it looks deletable, the census or measurement that would confirm it, and the date seen. Tony decides the cuts, one cleanup pass at a time.

